    "code":  "ALCOHOLIC_HEPATITIS_WITH_ASCITES",
    "name":  "Alcoholic hepatitis with ascites",
    "module":  "hepatobiliary",
    "category":  "disease",
    "description":  "Alcoholic hepatitis with ascites represents a more severe form of alcoholic hepatitis in which portal hypertension has developed sufficiently to cause peritoneal fluid accumulation. Ascites in this context signals advanced hepatic dysfunction with reduced albumin synthesis and elevated sinusoidal pressure. These patients are at high risk for spontaneous bacterial peritonitis (SBP), hepatorenal syndrome, and variceal bleeding. The combination of acute-on-chronic liver injury with ascites carries a substantially higher 90-day mortality than alcoholic hepatitis alone.",
